contract:
{
  "interface": {
    "mode": "functional",
    "class_name": null,
    "function_name": "findMirror",
    "signature": "root: TreeNode, target: int -> int"
  },
  "preconditions": [
    {
      "id": "P1",
      "expression": "isinstance(root, TreeNode) or root is None",
      "description": "The root is either a TreeNode or None."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "expression": "isinstance(target, int)",
      "description": "The target is an integer."
    }
  ],
  "postconditions": [
    {
      "id": "Q1",
      "expression": "return_value == -1 or (isinstance(return_value, int) and 1 <= return_value <= 10**4)",
      "description": "The return value is either -1 or an integer between 1 and 10^4."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2",
      "expression": "return_value == -1 or (exists_mirror(root, target, return_value))",
      "description": "The return value is -1 if the mirror node does not exist, otherwise it is the value of the mirror node."
    }
  ],
  "invariants": []
}

Note: The `exists_mirror` function is a semantic helper that checks if the mirror node of the target exists and has the return value. It is not a built-in function and should be defined based on the logic of finding the mirror node in the binary tree.
